check-memory-gate: ok c suppression: tests/guix-glibc-locpath.supp holds exactly one entry, guix-glibc-locpath, a definite leak under compute_locale_search_path
check-memory-gate: ok d used: a run that loads libcurl through (curl) passes, and Valgrind reports guix-glibc-locpath used on one block
check-memory-gate: ok d needed: without the suppression, the same run fails on the one block lost under compute_locale_search_path
check-memory-gate: ok d leak: the leak plant fails with the suppression read
check-memory-gate: ok d more: a second block lost under newlocale, which the entry matches, fails the suite
check-memory-gate: ok d alone: one block lost under newlocale in a run that loads no libcurl, and so no p11-kit, fails the suite
check-memory-gate: ok d override: MEMORY_SUPPRESSION_FILE on make's command line, naming a file that hides the overrun plant, is ignored, so the plant fails
