check-memory-gate: ok j evidence: a CHEZ that is a script running Chez as a child fails the leak plant, which Valgrind never saw
check-memory-gate: ok j evidence: a program that execs away from Valgrind, which then reports nothing, fails
check-memory-gate: ok j evidence: a Valgrind that runs another program than the suite fails the suite
check-memory-gate: ok k undef: a program that branches on memory nothing initialised fails, exit 9, with Valgrind's report: the plant the next case hides
check-memory-gate: ok k added: --undef-value-errors=no, added through VALGRIND, hides that plant, and fails it by name
check-memory-gate: ok k dropped: a Valgrind that drops --leak-check=full hides the leak plant, and fails it by name
check-memory-gate: ok k changed: a Valgrind that turns --errors-for-leak-kinds=definite to none hides the leak plant, and fails it by name
check-memory-gate: ok k order: a Valgrind that moves --leak-check=full to the end of its options fails a clean program, by name
check-memory-gate: ok l forged: a suite that prints a clean ERROR SUMMARY with Valgrind's pid, then execs away, fails: the evidence is Valgrind's own log
check-memory-gate: ok l stale: a Valgrind log an earlier run left is never read: a Valgrind that writes none fails
check-memory-gate: ok l names: two suites with one name, in two directories, are refused, so one suite's logs are never another's
check-memory-gate: ok m awk: an awk that fails, printing nothing, fails a clean program, naming the evidence check
check-memory-gate: ok m awk: an awk that prints ok, then exits 2, fails a clean program, naming the evidence check
check-memory-gate: ok m awk: an awk that exits 0, printing nothing, fails a clean program, naming the evidence check
